Random32 is Thumb assembly in a naked function, which clang cannot compile for wasm32. Under
IRV_WASM the function goes, and the glue's C Random32 (rom/gen3/wasm/src/irv_wasm_replace.c)
takes its place at link time. Every other function of the file stays, so Random(),
RandomUniform, the Shuffle functions and AdvanceRandom call the glue's Random32 and step
gRngValue as on the GBA.

diff --git a/src/random.c b/src/random.c
index 16de435..8ee1249 100644
--- a/src/random.c
+++ b/src/random.c
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ static void SFC32_Seed(struct Sfc32State *state, u32 seed, u8 stream)
 /*This ASM implementation uses some shortcuts and is generally faster on the GBA.
 * It's not necessarily faster if inlined, or on other platforms.
 * In addition, it's extremely non-portable. */
+#ifndef IRV_WASM
 u32 NAKED Random32(void)
 {
     asm(".thumb\n\
@@ -69,6 +70,7 @@ u32 NAKED Random32(void)
     .ltorg"
     );
 }
+#endif
 
